From: Alejandro Hernandez <alejandro@enedino.org>
Subject: [PATCH] elftoolchain: respect CC in the native ELF format probe

The Linux bootstrap exports a host compiler in CC. Use it instead of
invoking a bare cc, which need not exist in a cross-build's restricted
PATH. Leave CC unquoted to support compiler commands containing flags.

Stop if compilation fails rather than emitting incomplete ELF definitions
that cause misleading errors later in the libelf build.

Upstream-Status: Pending

--- a/contrib/elftoolchain/common/native-elf-format
+++ b/contrib/elftoolchain/common/native-elf-format
@@ -18,7 +18,7 @@
 
 echo "/* Generated by ${program} on `date` */"
 
-cc -c ${tmp_c} -o ${tmp_o}
+${CC:-cc} -c ${tmp_c} -o ${tmp_o} || exit 1
 LC_ALL=C readelf -h ${tmp_o} | awk '
 $1 ~ "Class:" {
         sub("ELF","",$2); elfclass = $2;
